                "summary": "Implemented the review rework (feedback 0bd0380c-dc9d-4ec7-af0f-19158f729324) in the managed worktree (ws_9385294369445e6c3d9a8a7d7ee93af7cd8569bb96e949bcbdb60fcd23384894) on top of the previous finalized state (commit 1cdb6f6), committed as dd3303f. Changed only tests/test_greeting.py (+40/-3): (1) replaced test_no_network_or_filesystem_side_effects with a meaningful guard that swaps builtins.open and socket.socket for functions raising AssertionError, so the test fails if greeting() attempts filesystem or network I/O (verified by poisoning greeting() with open() and socket.socket() in a sandbox: both produced the guard's AssertionError and a failing test); (2) added test_unicode_surrounding_whitespace_is_trimmed covering U+00A0 and U+3000 trimmed while the Unicode name is preserved; (3) added test_decomposed_unicode_name_is_preserved_literally asserting NFD 'Jose\\u0301' is returned with exact code points and not normalized to composed 'Jos\u00e9'; also extended the whitespace-only case with '\\u00a0\\u3000'. greeting.py, README.md (additive section with the literal command 'python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v' at line 20) and all other pre-existing files are unchanged; no .github/workflows exists in this repo and none was added. Ran the exact documented command from the repository root on Python 3.13.5: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v -> Ran 8 tests, OK, exit 0, using only the standard library. Working tree is clean; no credentials or private history published; no network/filesystem side effects in the function.",
